meta {
  name: Send Bulk Email
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/bulk-email
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

body:multipart-form {
  subject: Semester registration closes Friday
  body: <p>Dear student,</p><p>Registration for the coming semester closes on Friday at 5pm.</p>
  selections: [{"type":"Student","guids":["628B6873-7634-43A2-9101-F73D8B36FAAD","8B3249D4-E8F6-4308-AB3D-58E41754B6F9"]}]
  ~file: @file(C:\path\to\circular.pdf)
}

docs {
  Queues one bulk email send. Returns immediately with a job GUID — nothing is sent during this
  request. Two background workers do the rest: an expander turns the selected GUIDs into rows in
  OutboundEmails, then the outbound dispatcher drains that table at the configured SES rate.

  OutboundEmails carries every email in the system, not just bulk — OTPs and password-setup links
  land there at a higher Priority and preempt a running bulk job, so a large circular never delays
  a password reset.

  selections: a JSON array, one entry per recipient type, sent as a single form field (the nested
  shape does not survive repeated-form-field binding). Each entry is
  `{"type": "Student" | "Employee", "guids": [...]}`. One job can mix both types — the type lives on
  the recipient row, not the job. Duplicate GUIDs are collapsed server-side before insert.

  Only the Student resolver is implemented today; an Employee selection fails expansion with
  "No recipient resolver is registered for type 'Employee'" and the job is marked Failed.

  file: optional, disabled by default (prefixed with ~). Enable it and point it at a real file to
  test an upload. NOTE: the object is uploaded and recorded, but the download link is not yet
  appended to the email body and there is no endpoint serving it — recipients currently have no way
  to reach an attached file. Send without a file until that lands.

  selectedRecipients in the response is how many GUIDs were accepted, NOT how many emails will be
  sent. Students whose application record has no email address are dropped during expansion, so the
  delivered count is usually lower.

  There is no CANCEL endpoint, but progress can be read back: List Bulk Emails, Get Bulk Email
  (job + rendered body + counters), and Get Bulk Email Recipients (per-person outcomes). The
  BulkEmailJobs / OutboundEmails tables and the logs remain the ground truth.

  Success (201): `data` is `{ jobGuid, selectedRecipients }`.
  Failures: 400 validation_error — subject/body missing, subject > 998 chars, selections missing or
  not valid JSON, no recipients selected, more than 10000 recipients, attachment empty/over 8 MB/
  disallowed MIME type, or attachment file name missing or > 260 chars.
  400 bad_request — the caller has no X-User-Guid (the job records who created it).
  401 unauthorized — no valid erp_access cookie.
}
